course: dictionary
lesson: 10062
title: One word, two jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. Tetra is a noun for a small, brightly coloured fish, and it is also a prefix, a little piece added to the start of a longer word. «Mexican tetra fish trapped in dark caves evolved to lose their eyes and colour» uses tetra as the name of a fish.
explain: When tetra- starts a longer word, it means four. A tetrahedron is a solid with four faces, and a tetrapod is an animal with four limbs. So if you see tetra- at the front of an unknown word, pause and ask: could this be about the number four?
explain: Context tells you which meaning to use. «Tropical fish such as angelfish and neon tetras need warm water kept steady by a heater» has other fish all around it, so tetras here are fish. Check by swapping in your meaning and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A tetra is a small, often brightly coloured freshwater fish.
fact: Tetras are popular in home aquariums, such as the neon tetra.
fact: Tetra- at the start of a word means four.
fact: «Tetrahedron» means a solid with four faces.
fact: «Tetrapod» means an animal with four limbs.
exercise: «Tropical fish such as angelfish and neon tetras need warm water.» What is a tetra in this sentence? | A warm tank heater | A kind of cool water | *A small freshwater fish
exercise: Tetra- at the start of a word means what? | Two | Ten | Three | *Four
exercise: What is a tetrahedron? | A kind of cave | *A solid with four faces | A four-legged animal | A fish with fins
test: «Mexican tetra fish trapped in dark caves evolved to lose their eyes.» Why did they lose their eyes? | *Eyes were useless in darkness and cost energy | They wanted to see better in the dark | They were tired of looking at the cave walls
test: A tetrapod is an animal with how many limbs? | *Four | Two | Six | Eight
exam: In «tetrapod», which part of the word means four? | -pod | *tetra- | Both parts | Neither part
